docs {
  # Clinical Co-Pilot API collection

  Run top to bottom ("Run collection"). Requests 3-6 establish the admin
  session and capture the CSRF token and facts hash into variables that the
  later requests use; 13-16 start a second session as a restricted user.

   1. Health                    liveness, no auth
   2. Ready                     dependency probes, no auth, cached 60s
   3. Login page                starts the OpenEMR session
   4. Login                     authenticates (admin by default)
   5. Open chart                sets the session patient; captures csrf_token
   6. Brief                     the verified briefing; captures facts_hash
   7. Ask                       a cited follow-up
   8. Ask for arithmetic        withheld: declined or stripped (eval case 11)
   9. Ask outside the window    not_in_facts (eval case 10)
  10. Ask with stale hash       chart_changed: true
  11. Brief again               cache hit, zero tokens
  12. Brief without CSRF        403
  13-15. Restricted user        new session, login, open chart
  16. Restricted user brief     403 "You are not authorized to view this chart"

  Select the `local` or `vps` environment. The collection captures the
  session cookie itself (run the CLI with --disable-cookies). The patient id
  comes from the OpenEMR session set in request 5; a pid in the chat body is
  ignored by design.
}
